      },
      "message": "fix(post): the PathPilot lathe G76 refuses a repeat of each depth\n\nMain's #612 Tormach lathe post writes a one-block LinuxCNC G76. Its\ng76Why did not read RepeatEachDepth, so a plan that repeats each\nroughing depth posted a cycle that cuts each depth once - not the\npasses that were verified. It now refuses by name, the same rule as\nfanuc-lathe.cps and as alternating infeed. G33 passes still post the\nrepeat.\n\nPinned by a new case in lathe_post_tormach_thread::\na_g76_record_the_cycle_cannot_state_exactly_is_refused_by_name.\n\nRefs #418\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus <noreply@anthropic.com>",
